S167 cocycle normal-form atlas for LRC14
======================================================

[1] Exact definitions
---------------------
Proof packet complex P:
  vertices: labelled proof states, not automatically runners
  edges: admissible quotient, handoff, wall-crossing, or comparison moves
  2-cells: commuting proof squares, Haar squares, tournament triples, chart overlaps
Coefficient groups:
  integers/rationals for counts and moments; signs for topes; characters for periods
Cochain:
  a k-observable a assigns a value to k-cells of P
Cocycle condition:
  delta a = 0 on all cells whose boundary preserves the target LRC predicate
Coboundary/certificate condition:
  a = delta phi on a quotient fiber, or a dual certificate annihilates a
Sound quotient condition:
  every forgotten direction is fiber-constant, reconstructed, dual-annihilated,
  or mapped to a named residual group such as F7/THM-572.

[2] Cocycle carriers
--------------------
- labelled_packet_total_cocycle [mixed total class]
  base: LRC proof-packet complex: rows, endpoint cells, exact M/Farey node, proof exits
  cochain: all retained labels as one packet cochain
  delta law: delta(packet)=0 on every declared commuting proof square
  exit: fiber-constant, reconstructed, dual-annihilated, or routed to named residual
  LRC pull: normal form: every usable quotient must say where each forgotten direction went
  first nonzero family: not a residual family; this is the bookkeeping object
  anchors: HYP-2996, HYP-2995, HYP-2994, HYP-2992, HYP-2990, HYP-2991, HYP-2987, LTI-147
  retention vector: predicate=5, base_fiber=5, gauge_invariance=5, coboundary_test=5, dual_annihilator=5, local_to_global=5, formalizable=5, residual_named=5, anti_scalar_guard=5
- haar_zipper_2cocycle [2-cocycle / square curl]
  base: 2 x 2 Haar or fixed-margin tournament square
  cochain: zeta(T)=T00-T01-T10+T11
  delta law: fixed row/column margins imply only the mixed curl can move
  exit: orthogonal cancellation, boundary stop, owner strip, cross handoff, nested descent, F7
  LRC pull: row/column margins are unsafe unless zeta is retained or discharged
  first nonzero family: F_zeta: unpaired mixed Haar curl after all zipper teeth fail
  anchors: HYP-2991, HYP-2989, HYP-2595
  retention vector: predicate=5, base_fiber=5, gauge_invariance=4, coboundary_test=5, dual_annihilator=4, local_to_global=5, formalizable=4, residual_named=5, anti_scalar_guard=5
- endpoint_owner_boundary_cocycle [1-cocycle / boundary current]
  base: regular-open circle cells cut by danger endpoints
  cochain: signed endpoint owner current on the tope boundary graph
  delta law: boundary owner current sums to zero around closed equality atoms
  exit: AP/GW boundary cocircuit, open tope, or named wall residual
  LRC pull: separates positive strict witnesses from closed endpoint-only atoms
  first nonzero family: F_wall: no open tope and no AP/GW boundary cocircuit
  anchors: HYP-2986, HYP-2984, HYP-2949
  retention vector: predicate=5, base_fiber=5, gauge_invariance=4, coboundary_test=5, dual_annihilator=3, local_to_global=4, formalizable=5, residual_named=5, anti_scalar_guard=5
- farey_excess_mediant_1cocycle [1-cocycle / determinant defect]
  base: Farey edge path adjacent to 1/14
  cochain: e(p/q)=14p-q and det((p,q),(p',q'))
  delta law: mediant addition preserves primitive edge data only with determinant labels
  exit: e=0 AP/GW equality, e=1 unit-excess child, e>1 non-tight branch
  LRC pull: binding scale is q plus Farey excess, not product or numerator scalar alone
  first nonzero family: F_farey: first nonzero excess class beyond the 1/14 boundary
  anchors: HYP-2930, HYP-2931, HYP-2932, HYP-2945
  retention vector: predicate=5, base_fiber=5, gauge_invariance=5, coboundary_test=4, dual_annihilator=3, local_to_global=5, formalizable=5, residual_named=5, anti_scalar_guard=5
- c27_carry_lift_1cocycle [1-cocycle / covering carry]
  base: C27 antipodal shell cover over residues
  cochain: carry k in v=r+27k, plus gcd shell route
  delta law: lift changes must preserve shell route and unit/nonunit monodromy
  exit: unit petal discharge, GW D3 branch, K33 D9 state-lift debt
  LRC pull: residue shadows lie unless the carry and gcd-shell route are retained
  first nonzero family: F_carry: nonunit C27 monodromy, usually K33/D9
  anchors: HYP-2937, HYP-2942, HYP-2171
  retention vector: predicate=5, base_fiber=5, gauge_invariance=5, coboundary_test=4, dual_annihilator=3, local_to_global=4, formalizable=4, residual_named=5, anti_scalar_guard=5
- fejer_toeplitz_dual_coboundary [dual coboundary / PSD annihilator]
  base: Fourier moment cone of the danger multiplicity C_S(t)-1
  cochain: finite Toeplitz moment functional or Fejer trigonometric square
  delta law: covering would force every Toeplitz moment matrix to be PSD
  exit: negative Fejer/Toeplitz certificate is a dual coboundary for a safe interval
  LRC pull: low harmonic PSD failure is a certificate, not just a numerical shadow
  first nonzero family: F_psd: harmonic moment cone fails to certify or fails to descend
  anchors: HYP-2974, HYP-2981, HYP-2987
  retention vector: predicate=5, base_fiber=4, gauge_invariance=4, coboundary_test=5, dual_annihilator=5, local_to_global=4, formalizable=5, residual_named=4, anti_scalar_guard=5
- ramanujan_exact_period_character_cocycle [1-cocycle / exact-period character]
  base: denominator and divisor lattice of primitive periods
  cochain: Ramanujan exact-period packet c_q(a-b) with Mobius inversion labels
  delta law: period projectors commute only when prime-power and endpoint labels are kept
  exit: exact-period projector, prime-power side channel, or smoothing handoff
  LRC pull: divisor quotients are unsafe without endpoint, qdiv, and prime-power labels
  first nonzero family: F_period: exact-period character survives divisor quotient
  anchors: HYP-2978, HYP-2979, HYP-2982
  retention vector: predicate=4, base_fiber=4, gauge_invariance=5, coboundary_test=4, dual_annihilator=4, local_to_global=4, formalizable=5, residual_named=4, anti_scalar_guard=5
- tope_cocircuit_wall_cocycle [oriented matroid cocycle]
  base: hyperplane arrangement of danger endpoints
  cochain: tope sign vector and boundary cocircuit owner pair
  delta law: crossing a wall changes one sign and records the cocircuit
  exit: open all-safe tope, AP/GW equality cocircuit, or forbidden wall packet
  LRC pull: closed boundary debt and open witness mass must not be scalarized together
  first nonzero family: F_cocircuit: wall packet not discharged by open-tope or equality atom
  anchors: HYP-2986, HYP-2948, HYP-2951
  retention vector: predicate=5, base_fiber=5, gauge_invariance=4, coboundary_test=5, dual_annihilator=3, local_to_global=4, formalizable=5, residual_named=5, anti_scalar_guard=5
- tournament_path_h1_cocycle [1-cocycle modulo coboundaries]
  base: tournament path-homology or proof-carrier tournament
  cochain: edge comparison weights; triangle curl records nontransitive pressure
  delta law: transitive triples kill curl; directed 3-cycles expose H^1/H^2 pressure
  exit: score potential coboundary, SCC support residue, or named cyclic obstruction
  LRC pull: tournament iso classes help only after the quotient states what labels survived
  first nonzero family: F_tournament: non-potential tournament pressure class
  anchors: beta1_upper_bound, HYP-2924, HYP-2990
  retention vector: predicate=4, base_fiber=3, gauge_invariance=4, coboundary_test=5, dual_annihilator=2, local_to_global=4, formalizable=4, residual_named=4, anti_scalar_guard=4
- boundary_moment_multichart_cocycle [chart-transition cocycle]
  base: adaptive exact-period boundary-moment charts
  cochain: missed-sector depth vector across denominator charts
  delta law: one all-covered chart is harmless unless transition data also closes
  exit: multi-chart feasible region, positive Haar image, or K33/state-lift debt
  LRC pull: covering residuals need chart identity and transition labels
  first nonzero family: F_chart: boundary-moment transition class fails to close
  anchors: HYP-2969, HYP-2965, HYP-2968
  retention vector: predicate=4, base_fiber=5, gauge_invariance=4, coboundary_test=3, dual_annihilator=4, local_to_global=4, formalizable=3, residual_named=5, anti_scalar_guard=5
- state_lift_obstruction_class [named residual cohomology class]
  base: TournamentStateLift / THM-572 residual sector
  cochain: packet value agreeing with forbidden H=7 lift
  delta law: all lower exits failed and the residual must be represented in the lift
  exit: construct forbidden state lift or split the residual into earlier cocycles
  LRC pull: F7 is not an exception bucket; it must be a named obstruction class
  first nonzero family: F_lift: irreducible named state-lift obstruction
  anchors: THM-572, HYP-2908, HYP-2963, LTI-039, HYP-2987, HYP-2991
  retention vector: predicate=5, base_fiber=4, gauge_invariance=5, coboundary_test=3, dual_annihilator=3, local_to_global=5, formalizable=5, residual_named=5, anti_scalar_guard=5
- curried_section_derivative_cocycle [1-cocycle / section derivative]
  base: curried proof maps after freezing runners, endpoints, modes, or packet coordinates
  cochain: difference between adjacent sections of a partially applied proof function
  delta law: section derivatives must commute around frozen-coordinate squares
  exit: reconstruct forgotten coordinate, prove section independence, or expose defect
  LRC pull: curried functions are useful exactly when their section derivative is controlled
  first nonzero family: F_section: frozen-coordinate derivative refuses to commute
  anchors: HYP-2990, LRC technique index, curried-functions thread
  retention vector: predicate=4, base_fiber=4, gauge_invariance=5, coboundary_test=4, dual_annihilator=3, local_to_global=4, formalizable=3, residual_named=4, anti_scalar_guard=5
- raw_scalar_shadow [0-shadow / negative control]
  base: unlabelled scalar summaries
  cochain: one number such as residue class count, component count, or product value
  delta law: none without an external theorem identifying the kernel
  exit: diagnostic only after cocycle channels are already discharged
  LRC pull: explains why residue, product, component, and iso-class shadows keep lying
  first nonzero family: not a family; this is the anti-template
  anchors: HYP-2990, HYP-2991, HYP-2978
  retention vector: predicate=2, base_fiber=1, gauge_invariance=1, coboundary_test=1, dual_annihilator=1, local_to_global=1, formalizable=1, residual_named=1, anti_scalar_guard=1

